/**
@page api_algorithms Algorithm Modules
@brief PFQN, cache, MAM, queueing systems

These modules provide specialized algorithms for queueing network analysis.

@section alg_pfqn Product-Form Queueing Networks (matlab/src/api/pfqn/)

The pfqn module contains algorithms for product-form queueing networks, including
Mean Value Analysis (MVA), convolution, and normalizing constant methods.

@subsection alg_pfqn_functions Key Functions

<b>Primary Solvers:</b>
- @ref pfqn_aql.m "pfqn_aql" - Approximate Queue Length (AQL) algorithm for product-form networks.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [XN, QN, UN, RN, numIters, AN] = pfqn_aql(L, N, Z, TOL, MAXITER, QN0)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>TOL</td><td>Tolerance for convergence.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>MAXITER</td><td>Maximum number of iterations.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>QN0</td><td>Initial guess for queue lengths.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>XN</td><td>System throughput.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>QN</td><td>Mean queue lengths.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>UN</td><td>Utilization.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>RN</td><td>Residence times.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>numIters</td><td>Number of iterations.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>AN</td><td>Average arrival rate at nodes.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Approximate Queue Length (AQL) algorithm for product-form networks.

- @ref pfqn_bsfcfs.m "pfqn_bsfcfs" - Bard-Schweitzer approximate MVA for FCFS scheduling with weighted priorities.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [XN, QN, UN, RN, it] = pfqn_bsfcfs(L, N, Z, tol, maxiter, QN, weight)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector (default: zeros).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>tol</td><td>Convergence tolerance (default: 1e-6).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>maxiter</td><td>Maximum number of iterations (default: 1000).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>QN</td><td>Initial queue length matrix (default: uniform distribution).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>weight</td><td>Weight matrix for relative priorities (default: ones).</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>XN</td><td>System throughput.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>QN</td><td>Mean queue lengths.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>UN</td><td>Utilization.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>RN</td><td>Residence times.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>it</td><td>Number of iterations performed.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Bard-Schweitzer approximate MVA for FCFS scheduling with weighted priorities.

- @ref pfqn_bs.m "pfqn_bs" - Bard-Schweitzer Approximate Mean Value Analysis (MVA).

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [XN, QN, UN, RN, it] = pfqn_bs(L, N, Z, tol, maxiter, QN0, type)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>tol</td><td>Tolerance for convergence.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>maxiter</td><td>Maximum number of iterations.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>QN0</td><td>Initial guess for queue lengths.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>type</td><td>Scheduling strategy type (default: PS).</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>XN</td><td>System throughput.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>QN</td><td>Mean queue lengths.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>UN</td><td>Utilization.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>RN</td><td>Residence times.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>it</td><td>Number of iterations performed.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Bard-Schweitzer Approximate Mean Value Analysis (MVA).

- @ref pfqn_ca.m "pfqn_ca" - Convolution Algorithm for exact normalizing constant computation.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [Gn, lGn] = pfqn_ca(L, N, Z)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Gn</td><td>Normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>lGn</td><td>Logarithm of the normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Convolution Algorithm for exact normalizing constant computation.

- @ref pfqn_cdfun.m "pfqn_cdfun" - AMVA-QD class-dependence function for queue-dependent scaling.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  pfqn_cdfun(...)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> AMVA-QD class-dependence function for queue-dependent scaling.

- @ref pfqn_comom.m "pfqn_comom" - CoMoM algorithm for computing the normalizing constant.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  pfqn_comom(...)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> CoMoM algorithm for computing the normalizing constant.

- @ref pfqn_comomrm_ld.m "pfqn_comomrm_ld" - CoMoM for repairman model with load-dependent service rates.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [G, lG, prob] = pfqn_comomrm_ld(L, N, Z, mu, options)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>mu</td><td>Load-dependent rate matrix (MxNt matrix).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>options</td><td>Solver options.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>G</td><td>Normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>lG</td><td>Logarithm of normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>prob</td><td>State probability distribution.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> CoMoM for repairman model with load-dependent service rates.

- @ref pfqn_comomrm.m "pfqn_comomrm" - CoMoM (Convolution Method of Moments) for finite repairman model.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [lG, lGbasis] = pfqn_comomrm(L, N, Z, m, atol)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>m</td><td>Replication factor (default: 1).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>atol</td><td>Absolute tolerance for numerical computations.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>lG</td><td>Logarithm of normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>lGbasis</td><td>Logarithm of basis functions.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> CoMoM (Convolution Method of Moments) for finite repairman model.

- @ref pfqn_comomrm_ms.m "pfqn_comomrm_ms" - CoMoM for multiserver repairman model.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [G, lG, prob] = pfqn_comomrm_ms(L, N, Z, m, S)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>m</td><td>Replication factor (default: 1).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>S</td><td>Number of servers at queueing stations.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>G</td><td>Normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>lG</td><td>Logarithm of normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>prob</td><td>State probability distribution.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> CoMoM for multiserver repairman model.

- @ref pfqn_comomrm_orig.m "pfqn_comomrm_orig" - Original CoMoM implementation for finite repairman model.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  pfqn_comomrm_orig(...)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Original CoMoM implementation for finite repairman model.

- @ref pfqn_conwayms.m "pfqn_conwayms" - Multiserver Linearizer approximation (Conway 1989).

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [Q, U, R, C, X, totiter] = pfqn_conwayms(L, N, Z, nservers, type, tol, maxiter)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>nservers</td><td>Number of servers per station.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>type</td><td>Scheduling strategy type per station (default: FCFS).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>tol</td><td>Convergence tolerance (default: 1e-8).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>maxiter</td><td>Maximum number of iterations (default: 1000).</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Q</td><td>Mean queue lengths.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>U</td><td>Utilization.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>R</td><td>Residence times.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>C</td><td>Cycle times.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>X</td><td>System throughput.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>totiter</td><td>Total number of iterations.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Multiserver Linearizer approximation (Conway 1989).

- @ref pfqn_cub.m "pfqn_cub" - Cubature method for normalizing constant using Grundmann-Moeller rules.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [Gn, lGn] = pfqn_cub(L, N, Z, order, atol)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix (MxR).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector (1xR).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector (1xR).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>order</td><td>Degree of cubature rule (default: ceil((sum(N)-1)/2)).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>atol</td><td>Absolute tolerance (default: 1e-8).</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Gn</td><td>Estimated normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>lGn</td><td>Logarithm of normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Cubature method for normalizing constant using Grundmann-Moeller rules.

- @ref pfqn_egflinearizer.m "pfqn_egflinearizer" - Extended generalized fixed-point Linearizer approximation.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [Q, U, W, C, X, totiter] = pfqn_egflinearizer(L, N, Z, type, tol, maxiter, alpha)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>type</td><td>Scheduling strategy type per station.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>tol</td><td>Convergence tolerance (default: 1e-8).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>maxiter</td><td>Maximum number of iterations (default: 1000).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>alpha</td><td>Per-class scaling exponent vector.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Q</td><td>Mean queue lengths.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>U</td><td>Utilization.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>W</td><td>Waiting times.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>C</td><td>Cycle times.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>X</td><td>System throughput.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>totiter</td><td>Total iterations performed.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Extended generalized fixed-point Linearizer approximation.

- @ref pfqn_fnc.m "pfqn_fnc" - Generate load-dependent rates for functional server model f(n)=n+c.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [mu, c] = pfqn_fnc(alpha, c)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>alpha</td><td>Rate parameters (Mx N matrix).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>c</td><td>Constant offset parameter (default: auto-determined).</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>mu</td><td>Load-dependent service rates.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>c</td><td>Determined offset constant.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Generate load-dependent rates for functional server model f(n)=n+c.

- @ref pfqn_gflinearizer.m "pfqn_gflinearizer" - Generalized fixed-point Linearizer with uniform scaling exponent.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [Q, U, W, C, X, totiter] = pfqn_gflinearizer(L, N, Z, type, tol, maxiter, alpha)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>type</td><td>Scheduling strategy type per station.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>tol</td><td>Convergence tolerance.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>maxiter</td><td>Maximum number of iterations.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>alpha</td><td>Uniform scaling exponent for all classes.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Q</td><td>Mean queue lengths.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>U</td><td>Utilization.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>W</td><td>Waiting times.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>C</td><td>Cycle times.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>X</td><td>System throughput.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>totiter</td><td>Total iterations performed.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Generalized fixed-point Linearizer with uniform scaling exponent.

- @ref pfqn_gld.m "pfqn_gld" - Exact normalizing constant for load-dependent queueing networks.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [G, lG] = pfqn_gld(L, N, mu, options)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix (MxR).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector (1xR).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>mu</td><td>Load-dependent rate matrix (Mx sum(N)).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>options</td><td>Solver options.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>G</td><td>Normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>lG</td><td>Logarithm of normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Exact normalizing constant for load-dependent queueing networks.

- @ref pfqn_gldsingle.m "pfqn_gldsingle" - Exact normalizing constant for single-class load-dependent models.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [lG, G] = pfqn_gldsingle(L, N, mu, options)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand vector (Mx1).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population (scalar).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>mu</td><td>Load-dependent rate matrix (MxN).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>options</td><td>Solver options.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>lG</td><td>Logarithm of normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>G</td><td>Normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Exact normalizing constant for single-class load-dependent models.

- @ref pfqn_grnmol.m "pfqn_grnmol" - Normalizing constant using Grundmann-Moeller quadrature.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  pfqn_grnmol(...)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Normalizing constant using Grundmann-Moeller quadrature.

- @ref pfqn_joint.m "pfqn_joint" - Compute joint queue-length probability distribution.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [F, A] = pfqn_joint(L, N, m)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>m</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>F</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  <tr><td>A</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Compute joint queue-length probability distribution.

- @ref pfqn_kt.m "pfqn_kt" - Knessl-Tier asymptotic expansion for normalizing constant.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [G, lG, X, Q] = pfqn_kt(L, N, Z)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector (default: zeros).</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>G</td><td>Normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>lG</td><td>Logarithm of normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>X</td><td>System throughput.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Q</td><td>Mean queue lengths.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Knessl-Tier asymptotic expansion for normalizing constant.

- @ref pfqn_lap.m "pfqn_lap" - Laplace approximation for normalizing constant.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  logI = pfqn_lap(L, N, Z)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>logI</td><td>Logarithm of normalizing constant approximation.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Laplace approximation for normalizing constant.

- @ref pfqn_lcfsqn_ca.m "pfqn_lcfsqn_ca" - Convolution algorithm for 2-station LCFS queueing networks

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [G, V] = pfqn_lcfsqn_ca(alpha, beta, N)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>alpha</td><td>Service rates at LCFS station (1xR vector).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>beta</td><td>Service rates at LCFS-PR station (1xR vector).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector (default: ones(1,R)).</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>G</td><td>Normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>V</td><td>Auxiliary normalization term.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Convolution algorithm for 2-station LCFS queueing networks

- @ref pfqn_lcfsqn_mva.m "pfqn_lcfsqn_mva" - Exact MVA for 2-station LCFS queueing networks.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [T, Q, U, B] = pfqn_lcfsqn_mva(alpha, beta, N)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>alpha</td><td>Service rates at LCFS station (1xR vector).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>beta</td><td>Service rates at LCFS-PR station (1xR vector).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector (default: ones(1,R)).</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>T</td><td>Throughput vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Q</td><td>Mean queue lengths (2xR matrix).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>U</td><td>Utilization (2xR matrix).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>B</td><td>Back probability matrix (2xR).</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Exact MVA for 2-station LCFS queueing networks.

