- @ref pfqn_ncld.m "pfqn_ncld" - Normalizing constant for load-dependent closed networks.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [lG, G, method] = pfqn_ncld(L, N, Z, mu, varargin)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>mu</td><td>Load-dependent rate matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>options</td><td>Optional solver parameters.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>lG</td><td>Logarithm of normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>G</td><td>Normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>method</td><td>Method used for computation.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Normalizing constant for load-dependent closed networks.

- @ref pfqn_nc.m "pfqn_nc" - Computes the normalizing constant of a product-form queueing network.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [lG, X, Q, method] = pfqn_nc(lambda, L, N, Z, varargin)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>lambda</td><td>Arrival rates for open classes.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>options</td><td>Optional arguments for solver options (NC.defaultOptions).</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>lG</td><td>Logarithm of the normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>X</td><td>System throughputs.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Q</td><td>Mean queue lengths.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>method</td><td>The specific method used for computation (e.g., 'exact', 'ca', 'recal').</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Computes the normalizing constant of a product-form queueing network.

- @ref pfqn_nc_sanitize.m "pfqn_nc_sanitize" - Sanitize and preprocess network parameters for NC solvers.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
