@section alg_mam Matrix-Analytic Methods (matlab/src/api/mam/)

The mam module implements matrix-analytic methods for analyzing queues with
structured Markov chains, including QBD, MAP, RAP, and G/M/1 and M/G/1 type processes.

@subsection alg_mam_functions Key Functions

<b>QBD Methods:</b>
- @ref aph_bernstein.m "aph_bernstein" - Fits an APH distribution using Bernstein's approximation

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  APH = aph_bernstein(f, order)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>f</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  <tr><td>order</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>APH</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Fits an APH distribution using Bernstein's approximation

- @ref map_ccdf_derivative.m "map_ccdf_derivative" - Derivative at zero of a MAP CCDF

  <b>Syntax:</b>
