@section alg_mc Markov Chain Utilities (matlab/lib/kpctoolbox/mc/)

Utilities for continuous-time and discrete-time Markov chains.

@subsection alg_mc_functions Key Functions

<b>CTMC Functions:</b>
- @ref ctmc_makeinfgen.m "ctmc_makeinfgen" - Normalizes a matrix to be a valid infinitesimal generator

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  ctmc_makeinfgen(...)
  @endcode

  <b>Description:</b> Normalizes a matrix to be a valid infinitesimal generator

- @ref ctmc_rand.m "ctmc_rand" - Generates a random infinitesimal generator matrix

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  ctmc_rand(...)
  @endcode

  <b>Description:</b> Generates a random infinitesimal generator matrix

- @ref ctmc_randomization.m "ctmc_randomization" - Uniformization (randomization) of a continuous-time Markov chain

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [P, q] = ctmc_randomization(Q, q)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Q</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  <tr><td>q</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>P</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  <tr><td>q</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Uniformization (randomization) of a continuous-time Markov chain

- @ref ctmc_relsolve.m "ctmc_relsolve" - Computes the equilibrium distribution relative to a reference state

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [p, Q, nConnComp, connComp] = ctmc_relsolve(Q, refstate, options)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Q</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  <tr><td>refstate</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  <tr><td>options</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>p</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Q</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  <tr><td>nConnComp</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  <tr><td>connComp</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Computes the equilibrium distribution relative to a reference state

- @ref ctmc_solve.m "ctmc_solve" - Equilibrium distribution of the continuous-time Markov chain

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [p, Q, nConnComp, connComp] = ctmc_solve(Q, options)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Q</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  <tr><td>options</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>p</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Q</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  <tr><td>nConnComp</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  <tr><td>connComp</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Equilibrium distribution of the continuous-time Markov chain

- @ref ctmc_timereverse.m "ctmc_timereverse" - Computes the time-reversed generator of a CTMC

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  ctmc_timereverse(...)
  @endcode

  <b>Description:</b> Computes the time-reversed generator of a CTMC

- @ref ctmc_transient.m "ctmc_transient" - Transient analysis of a continuous-time Markov chain using ODE solvers

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [pi, t] = ctmc_transient(Q, pi0, t0, t1, useStiff, reltol, timestep)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Q</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
